// What a *developed* party is worth, against the same fight an undeveloped one
// takes. The one instrument for the level half of companion progression: a
// Kernel Ring raises a companion's ceiling from 6 to `absolute_companion_level_
// cap()`, and `balance_sim` cannot see the difference because it never clamps a
// companion to the live cap at all.
//
// **What this file cannot measure.** The bin plays the game's own All-Attack
// every round, so no companion Special ever fires — which means `Ability`,
// `Affinity` and `RoutineSlot` talents are invisible here, exactly as they are
// invisible to `balance_sim`. Three of the four talent node kinds therefore
// have only one instrument: playing this same scenario on the arena screen
// (`FERAL_DEV_ARENA=1 cargo run`, then [R] Arena, [L] this file), where a
// person presses the keys and the Specials land.
//
// **Read as a delta, never as an absolute.** Arena numbers compare within one
// build only — a moved baseline is a reshuffled RNG stream, not a difficulty
// change. The control is this file with the party at `level: 6`, run in the
// same build; see `docs/measurements/` for what that pair said.
(
    player: Fresh(level: 20, zone: 3),
    equip: [
        (item: "plasma_router", tier: 0),
        (item: "bastion_lattice", tier: 0),
        (item: "singularity_matrix", tier: 0),
    ],
    // Every ring open, which is what six lair guardians buys one program.
    // Same species and gear as `full-group.ron`'s party, so the two files
    // differ in exactly one thing.
    party: [
        (species: "scrapper", level: 12, equip: [
            (item: "arc_lance"), (item: "hardened_shell"),
        ]),
        (species: "scrapper", level: 12, equip: [
            (item: "arc_lance"), (item: "hardened_shell"),
        ]),
        (species: "scrapper", level: 12, equip: [
            (item: "arc_lance"), (item: "hardened_shell"),
        ]),
    ],
    opponents: [(species: "rootkit", count: 4)],
    reps: 50,
    seed: 7,
)
